# `adj[queue.shift()!]`, `nodes[ids.get(name)!]`, `a[b[i]!]`: the key is a number or `undefined`. Under "undefined", "null", "true" and "false" nothing can lie above a list or a view: they are closed keys of every
# locked prototype, as the names of numbers are. Such a key names an element, what the program laid on the list itself, or nothing, so nobody gets the list as `this`. The read let the list out, and every object in it.
# L0 .. L6 = the seven classes, each held by a list of its own that is read under one form of such a key.
# RUN: link layouts mechanisms=all
# CHECK: layout L0 changes=[] stays-with-compiled-code
# CHECK: layout L1 changes=[] stays-with-compiled-code
# CHECK: layout L2 changes=[] stays-with-compiled-code
# CHECK: layout L3 changes=[] stays-with-compiled-code
# CHECK: layout L4 changes=[] stays-with-compiled-code
# CHECK: layout L5 changes=[] stays-with-compiled-code
# CHECK: layout L6 changes=[] stays-with-compiled-code
